{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-02T09:18:08.631Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"7687d94a08e852f40579b9f7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-he6i"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Correct the closeout record: the upstream template SDK defect is mitigated, not fixed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Tracks gh:unbraind/pm-presets#184 (filed 2026-10-31, missed by the blind issue watch). The closeout of the upstream-template-defect item marked it delivered with PR #170 and listed it under CHANGELOG 'Fixed', but PR #170 only ships the package's fail-closed adapter mitigation: the host defects remain on upstream main (parseStoredTemplateOptions still assigns arbitrary accepted keys by indexed assignment into normalized, builtinTemplateDocument still indexes BUILTIN_TEMPLATES without an own-property check, and resolveTypeSynonym still indexes the ordinary-object synonym table — re-verified on upstream main 2026-11-02). The canonical item itself says the upstream follow-up stays open and requires host SDK/CLI own-key regression coverage before revisiting those refusals. Action: record a follow-up here that keeps the upstream fix open (watch upstream releases for own-key checks in template parsing and type synonyms), and correct the CHANGELOG wording from 'Fixed' to 'Mitigated (package-side)' so consumers do not read the host defect as repaired."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["closeout","gh:unbraind/pm-presets#184","upstream"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/creat